## Project Structure

```
bookmarkr/
├── backend/                   # FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2.x + Pydantic v2
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── api/               # Routers (bookmarks, tags, auth)
│   │   ├── models/            # SQLAlchemy models (Bookmark, Tag)
│   │   ├── schemas/           # Pydantic request/response schemas
│   │   ├── services/          # Business logic (search.py, …) — not in route handlers
│   │   ├── core/              # config, security, logging
│   │   ├── database.py        # Engine + session
│   │   └── main.py            # App entry point
│   ├── alembic/versions/      # Migrations
│   ├── tests/{unit,integration}/
│   └── CONTEXT.md             # Domain glossary — lazy-built per Phase 4
├── frontend/                  # React + TypeScript
│   └── src/{pages,components,services,styles,types,hooks}/
├── .github/workflows/         # CI (backend, frontend, security)
└── docker-compose.yml         # frontend, backend, postgres
```

### Key architectural flows

- **Request flow:** Frontend → API client → `/api/*` → FastAPI router → service → SQLAlchemy → PostgreSQL.
- **Auth flow:** Frontend obtains a JWT from the auth provider → backend validates via a `get_current_user` dependency → the user id scopes every query (tenant isolation).
- **Search flow:** `GET /bookmarks/search?q=` → `services/search.py` builds a ranked, tenant-scoped Postgres full-text query (see [ADR-0001](docs/decisions/0001-postgres-fts-over-elasticsearch.md)).

### Domain glossary
For the canonical domain terms (Bookmark, Tag, SearchQuery, with invariants), see `backend/CONTEXT.md`. For load-bearing architectural choices, see `karpathy-knowledge-base-example/docs/decisions/`.

### External integrations
| Service | Purpose | Config |
|---------|---------|--------|
| Auth provider (JWT) | Sign-in, token issuance | `AUTH_ISSUER`, `AUTH_AUDIENCE` |
| PostgreSQL | Primary datastore + full-text search | `DATABASE_URL` |

_(Replace with your real integrations. Provider-specific gotchas live in `karpathy-knowledge-base-example/docs/integrations/<provider>/gotchas.md`.)_

